# Artform UI system

If this task does **not** create or change a user-facing screen, ignore this file.

If it does — new page, existing page, dashboard, form, empty state, marketing shell, Operator Console, or internal tool — you are not inventing a look. You are configuring the Artform kit. Full playbook: `docs/ARTFORM_UI_SYSTEM.md`.

## Why this exists

Cursor has no visual canvas. Unconstrained CSS is why agent-built UIs look amateur next to Base44. Base44 looks good because it wires a **pre-built design system**. Artform's equivalent is already in this repo: **shadcn/ui (New York) + Tailwind + CSS variables + Inter/Syne**. Use that. Do not write a second stylesheet.

## Stack (do not substitute)

- **Components:** shadcn/ui at `@/components/ui/*`. Add missing pieces with `npx shadcn@latest add <name>` (non-interactive). Never hand-roll Button, Card, Dialog, Input, Select, Table, Tabs, Toast, Sheet, Dropdown.
- **Styling:** Tailwind utility classes only. No new CSS files, no CSS-in-JS, no MUI/Chakra/Ant, no inline `style={{ color: '#…' }}` except for truly dynamic values (chart series from data).
- **Color:** only semantic tokens — `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, `bg-destructive`, `ring-ring`. **Never invent hex or raw hsl.** Brand accent is the existing `--primary` teal.
- **Type:** body `font-inter` (or the default body font). Headings `font-syne tracking-tight`. Do not add a third font.
- **Icons:** `lucide-react` only.
- **Motion:** existing `framer-motion` + `tailwindcss-animate`. Subtle, 150–250ms, opacity/translate only. **No Magic UI / Aceternity / sparkle landings on operational tools.** Those libraries are allowed only on an explicit marketing/landing brief, and even then they must still use Artform tokens.

## Aesthetic (Apple-like, not "SaaS rainbow")

- One primary action per screen. Secondary actions are outline/ghost.
- Ample whitespace: page padding `px-4 md:px-6 py-8`, vertical rhythm `space-y-6` or `space-y-8`.
- Cards: `rounded-xl border border-border bg-card shadow-sm`. No heavy drop shadows, no neon glow on data pages (Tessa chat glow utilities stay on chat only).
- Density: comfortable, not cramped. Tables stay `text-sm` with `tabular-nums` for money and dates.
- Radius comes from `--radius` (0.75rem). Do not mix `rounded-sm` buttons with `rounded-3xl` cards on the same page.
- Light and dark both work through tokens. Do not hard-code `bg-white` or `bg-black`.
- Mobile first: tap targets ≥ 40px, no hover-only actions, stack columns under `md`.

## Layout (copy this skeleton)

```jsx
import { PageShell, PageHeader, MetricCard, EmptyState } from "@/components/artform";
// Tessa pages also keep PageNav for Back / Home.

<PageShell nav={/* PageNav on Tessa; App header on standalone apps */}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Optional section"
    title="Name of the decision this page supports"
    description="One sentence: what the user should do with what they see."
    action={/* one primary Button */}
  />
  {/* optional MetricCard row */}
  {/* one main Card or Table */}
  {/* EmptyState when there is nothing to show */}
</PageShell>
```

## Copy and information design

- Headline the **decision**, not the dataset. A correctly computed number that is wrong to act on is a defect.
- Empty, loading, and error states are first-class: `Skeleton` while loading, `EmptyState` when zero rows, `Alert` for failures with a retry.
- Do not decorate with gradients, glassmorphism, or decorative illustration unless the page is a marketing landing.

## Existing vs new repos

- **Tessa (`tessa-af`):** extend `@/components/ui` and `@/components/artform`. Do not run `shadcn init` again.
- **This template / any app created from it:** add missing shadcn pieces with `npx shadcn@latest add <name>`. Keep the tokens in `src/app/globals.css`. Do not invent a second palette.

## v0 (optional speed path)

If the human pastes a [v0.dev](https://v0.dev) shell: restyle it onto Artform tokens and shadcn primitives before wiring data. Do not keep v0's invented colors, fonts, or custom CSS.

## Auth (not optional on data screens)

A pretty shell is not permission to skip auth. **No screen that reads Artform data or calls a credentialed API ships without a server-side auth gate.** The browser never holds `SIDEKICK_API_SECRET`, Procore secrets, or Smartsheet tokens. Skipping Base44 hosting is allowed only for tools that hold **no** Artform data and call **no** credentialed endpoint. Anything that reads Sidekick or writes Procore/Smartsheet needs its own ADR with a named auth decision — this UI kit is not that decision.

## Done means

- Uses shadcn + tokens; no new palette.
- Readable at a glance on desktop and phone.
- Verified in the browser (or the closest substitute) including empty/error paths — not a single screenshot of the happy path.
